#: codec/1/255/0xff000/4
msgid ""
"Well, next time you see her, make sure she gets it.\n"
msgstr ""
"下次见到她，务必交给她。\n"

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/5
msgid ""
"Oh, yeah, sure.\n"
msgstr ""
"哦，好。\n"

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/6
msgid ""
"Better for you if she doesn't...\n"
msgstr ""
"她没看对你更好……\n"

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/7
#: codec/2/904/0x388570/1
#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/17
msgid ""
"Snake!\n"
msgstr ""
"SNAKE！\n"

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/9
msgid ""
"Tell me you didn't read the letter.\n"
msgstr ""
"别告诉我你看了那封信。\n"

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/10
msgid ""
"N-no...\n"
msgstr ""
"没、没有……\n"

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/11
msgid ""
"You did!\n"
msgstr ""
"你看了！\n"

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/12
msgid ""
"I mean...\n"
msgstr ""
"我是说……\n"

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/13
msgid ""
"You never know what kind of information could\n"
"affect the outcome of an operation, right?\n"
msgstr ""
"你永远不知道什么样的信息会\n"
"影响行动的结局，对吧？\n"

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/14
msgid ""
"So I...\n"
msgstr ""
"所以我……\n"

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/15
msgid ""
"So you read the letter. After I specifically told you\n"
"not to!\n"
msgstr ""
"所以你还是看了那封信。我明确\n"
"说过别看！\n"

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/16
msgid ""
"...What do you expect people to do when you tell\n"
"them not to read something...?\n"
msgstr ""
"……你叫别人别看某样东西时，\n"
"觉得他们会怎么做……？\n"

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/17
msgid ""
"I thought I knew you, Snake! I thought I could trust\n"
"you!!\n"
msgstr ""
"我以为我了解你，Snake！我以为能信\n"
"你！！\n"

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/18
msgid ""
"But now I see I was wrong!\n"
msgstr ""
"现在看来我错了！\n"

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/19
msgid ""
"...Look, I'm sorry. But I just don't get what you see\n"
"in her.\n"
msgstr ""
"……抱歉。可我不懂你看上\n"
"她哪点。\n"

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/20
msgid ""
"Well, I wouldn't expect a barbarian who opens\n"
msgstr ""
"哼，不指望拆信的野蛮人\n"

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/21
msgid ""
"other people's private correspondence to\n"
"understand.\n"
msgstr ""
"别人的私人信件\n"
"去理解。\n"

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/22
msgid ""
"Fine, then. Deliver it yourself.\n"
msgstr ""
"行，那你自己去送吧。\n"

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/23
msgid ""
"Huh?! N-no, I... No way, I could never...\n"
msgstr ""
"啊？！不、不行，我……我做不到……\n"

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/24
msgid ""
"You've got a long way to go, Huey...\n"
msgstr ""
"你还差得远呢，休伊……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 445..1476
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/0
msgid ""
"You ever see the movie \"2001: A Space Odyssey\"?\n"
msgstr ""
"你看过《2001太空漫游》吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 1476..1852
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/1
msgid ""
"Can't say I have.\n"
msgstr ""
"没看过。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 1852..3301
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/2
msgid ""
"Fantastic flick... The outer space special effects\n"
"are incredible enough,\n"
msgstr ""
"好片子……外太空特效\n"
"已经够惊艳了，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 3301..4263
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/3
msgid ""
"but the depiction of AI is what really stands out.\n"
msgstr ""
"但对AI的刻画才是真正的亮点。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 4263..4583
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/4
msgid ""
"There's an AI ?\n"
msgstr ""
"里面有AI？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 4583..6339
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/5
msgid ""
"Yeah. A spacecraft pilot AI called HAL. It plays a\n"
"major role in the story.\n"
msgstr ""
"对。航天器驾驶员AI，叫HAL。它在\n"
"故事里很重要。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 6339..6965
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/6
msgid ""
"Dr. Strangelove loves it, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"博士也喜欢。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 6965..7913
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/7
msgid ""
"Did I ever tell you about the time we first met up\n"
"in Costa Rica?\n"
msgstr ""
"我说过我们第一次见面的事吗\n"
"在哥斯达黎加？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 7913..8164
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/8
msgid ""
"No.\n"
msgstr ""
"没有。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 8164..8860
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/9
msgid ""
"You know how she hates men, right?\n"
msgstr ""
"你知道她多讨厌男人吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 8874..10114
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/10
msgid ""
"So we hadn't seen each other since NASA, and we\n"
"just weren't hitting it off...\n"
msgstr ""
"我们从NASA之后就再没见过面，而且我们\n"
"就是合不来……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 10142..11674
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/11
msgid ""
"until we started talking about HAL, and then she\n"
"started going off.\n"
msgstr ""
"直到我们聊起HAL，然后她\n"
"就开始滔滔不绝了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 11758..12608
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/12
msgid ""
"The way she talked about it was so intellectual.\n"
msgstr ""
"她谈起它的样子特别有学识。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 12650..14266
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/13
msgid ""
"The way she analyzed every plot detail, how\n"
"passionate she was about the AI...\n"
msgstr ""
"她分析每一个情节细节的方式，她对\n"
"AI的那份热情……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 14308..15018
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/14
msgid ""
"It made me fall for her all over again.\n"
msgstr ""
"让我又一次爱上了她。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 15018..15380
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/15
msgid ""
"Uh huh.\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 15380..16746
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/16
msgid ""
"You know what? Here's to HAL, for bringing her\n"
"and me closer together!\n"
msgstr ""
"你知道吗？为HAL干杯，感谢它让她\n"
"和我走得更近！\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 16760..18459
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/17
msgid ""
"You should ask her about \"2001,\" too. Then you'll\n"
"understand just how amazing she is.\n"
msgstr ""
"你也该问问她《2001》。然后你就\n"
"会明白她多厉害。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 18459..18836
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/18
msgid ""
"Amazing, huh...\n"
msgstr ""
"厉害……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 18836..19880
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/19
msgid ""
"HAL... Now there's a good name...\n"
msgstr ""
"HAL……这名字不错……\n"

#: codec/1/255/0xffda0/0
msgid ""
"The Pupa increases its mobility by using\n"
"compressed air to hover its rear section.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xffda0/1
msgid ""
"It moves by means of its treads and boosters.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xffda0/2
msgid ""
"Those boosters also provide the propulsion needed\n"
"for high-speed movement.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xffda0/3
msgid ""
"So if I take out the boosters, it won't be able to\n"
"charge?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xffda0/5
msgid ""
"I suppose you could also avoid its attacks by lying\n"
"down beneath it...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xffda0/6
msgid ""
"The Pupa is also equipped with electrical shock\n"
"units.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xffda0/7
msgid ""
"It uses these devices - they look like lightning rods\n"
"- to direct discharge.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/0
msgid ""
"Being an unmanned vehicle,\n"
msgstr ""
"作为无人载具，\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/1
msgid ""
"the Chrysalis can perform extreme G-force\n"
"maneuvers that standard aircraft can't.\n"
msgstr ""
"Chrysalis能够执行普通飞机无法做到的\n"
"极限G力机动。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/2
msgid ""
"It'll be difficult to counter-attack once it's coming\n"
"at you.\n"
msgstr ""
"一旦它朝你冲过来，就很难\n"
"反击了。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/3
msgid ""
"I should mention that it's also equipped with a\n"
"railgun.\n"
msgstr ""
"我应该提一下，它还配备了一门\n"
"轨道炮。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/4
msgid ""
"A what?\n"
msgstr ""
"装有什么？\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/5
msgid ""
"A weapon that fires rounds using electromagnetic\n"
"force in lieu of gunpowder.\n"
msgstr ""
"一种用电磁力而非火药\n"
"发射弹丸的武器。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/6
msgid ""
"Wait... An electric weapon?\n"
msgstr ""
"等等……电击武器？\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/7
msgid ""
"Not exactly. The rounds themselves are\n"
"conventional shells.\n"
msgstr ""
"不完全是。弹丸本身是\n"
"常规炮弹。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/8
msgid ""
"It creates force by running an electric current\n"
"through a magnetic field.\n"
msgstr ""
"它通过让电流穿过磁场\n"
"来产生力。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/9
msgid ""
"Fleming's left-hand rule - didn't they teach you that\n"
"at school?\n"
msgstr ""
"弗莱明左手定则——学校没教过你\n"
"这个吗？\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/10
msgid ""
"Not at mine.\n"
msgstr ""
"我学校没教。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/11
msgid ""
"Oh. Anyway, as the railgun uses electromagnetic\n"
"force,\n"
msgstr ""
"哦。总之，由于轨道炮使用电磁\n"
"力，\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/12
msgid ""
"it needs to charge before firing.\n"
msgstr ""
"开火前需要充能。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/13
msgid ""
"Once you see it starting to charge, take immediate\n"
"evasive action.\n"
msgstr ""
"一旦发现它开始充能，立即采取\n"
"回避行动。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/14
msgid ""
"Also, as with the Pupa, destroying the AI will put\n"
"the unit out of commission.\n"
msgstr ""
"另外，和蛹一样，摧毁AI会让\n"
"该单位瘫痪。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/15
msgid ""
"Do enough damage and it'll have to land.\n"
msgstr ""
"伤害够了它就得降落。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/16
msgid ""
"Use that opportunity to get in the AI pod.\n"
msgstr ""
"趁此机会进入AI舱。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/17
msgid ""
"Wait too long, and it'll start to repair itself.\n"
msgstr ""
"拖太久它会开始自我修复。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/18
msgid ""
"Be sure to shoot the hatch the moment it lands.\n"
msgstr ""
"降落的瞬间务必射击舱门。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/19
msgid ""
"I think I can handle that.\n"
msgstr ""
"这个我能应付。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/0
msgid ""
"During development, I had trouble figuring out how\n"
"to handle the Cocoon's excess heat.\n"
msgstr ""
"在开发过程中，我很难弄清楚如何\n"
"处理茧的多余热量。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/1
msgid ""
"I'm embarrassed to admit it, but the radiators are\n"
"most likely its weakest points.\n"
msgstr ""
"我很不好意思承认，但散热器\n"
"很可能是它最薄弱的部位。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/2
msgid ""
"They're not heavily armored, as heat wasn't\n"
"dissipating properly.\n"
msgstr ""
"它们没有厚重的装甲，因为热量无法\n"
"正常散发。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/3
msgid ""
"Where are they?\n"
msgstr ""
"在哪里？\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/4
msgid ""
"There are multiple radiators on the upper and\n"
"lower sections.\n"
msgstr ""
"在上部和\n"
"下部有多个散热器。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/5
msgid ""
"Just look for the exhaust fumes.\n"
msgstr ""
"找排气烟雾就行。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/6
msgid ""
"Only thing is, the upper radiators typically aren't\n"
"exposed.\n"
msgstr ""
"问题是，上部散热器通常不会\n"
"暴露。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/7
msgid ""
"You should probably shoot for the lower ones first.\n"
msgstr ""
"最好先打下面的。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/8
msgid ""
"You could move under its body to access the\n"
"lower ones,\n"
msgstr ""
"你可移到它身下接触\n"
"下部散热器，\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/9
msgid ""
"but the Cocoon is capable of vertical movement,\n"
"so be careful not to get crushed.\n"
msgstr ""
"但茧能够垂直移动，\n"
"所以小心不要被压扁。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/10
msgid ""
"Watch out for missiles and hedgehogs too.\n"
msgstr ""
"也要提防导弹和刺猬弹。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/11
msgid ""
"Hedgehogs? Anti-submarine multiple spigot\n"
"mortars?\n"
msgstr ""
"刺猬弹？反潜多管\n"
"迫击炮？\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/12
msgid ""
"I adapted the technology for use as a surface\n"
"weapon.\n"
msgstr ""
"我改造技术，用作水面\n"
"武器。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/13
msgid ""
"Both the missiles and hedgehogs take time to load,\n"
"though.\n"
msgstr ""
"不过，导弹和刺猬都需要时间\n"
"装填。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/14
msgid ""
"It can't fire a hedgehog until the lamp comes on.\n"
msgstr ""
"指示灯亮起前它无法发射刺猬弹。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/15
msgid ""
"As for the missiles, watch for the way the hatches\n"
"move.\n"
msgstr ""
"至于导弹，注意舱门\n"
"移动的方式。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/16
msgid ""
"That'll be my chance to get close.\n"
msgstr ""
"那就是我靠近的机会。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/17
msgid ""
"When the hatches open, out come the missiles.\n"
msgstr ""
"舱门一开，导弹就出来了。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/0
msgid ""
"...Number of warheads detected by the DEW Line?\n"
msgstr ""
"……预警线探测到的弹头数量？\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/1
msgid ""
"Fifty-seven.\n"
msgstr ""
"五十七枚。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/2
msgid ""
"Number of MIRVs included?\n"
msgstr ""
"分导多弹头多少？\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/3
msgid ""
"Minimum twenty-nine, maximum thirty-five.\n"
msgstr ""
"最少二十九，最多三十五。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/4
msgid ""
"Target region?\n"
msgstr ""
"目标区？\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/5
msgid ""
"United States. East Coast.\n"
msgstr ""
"美国。东海岸。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/6
msgid ""
"Estimated time of reentry?\n"
msgstr ""
"预计再入时间？\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/7
msgid ""
"Two-oh-four-eight Zulu.\n"
msgstr ""
"祖鲁时间二〇四八。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/8
msgid ""
"President's selected attack option?\n"
msgstr ""
"总统选定的攻击方案？\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/9
msgid ""
"Unknown.\n"
msgstr ""
"不明。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/10
msgid ""
"The President is dead?\n"
msgstr ""
"总统死了？\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/11
msgid ""
"Unknown. Communication has been lost.\n"
msgstr ""
"不明。通讯已中断。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/12
msgid ""
"...I select Offutt Air Force Base as my target.\n"
msgstr ""
"……我选奥福特空军基地为目标。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/13
msgid ""
"Offutt...? But that's a U.S. base! What on earth do\n"
"you mean?!\n"
msgstr ""
"奥福特……？那是美国基地！你什么\n"
"意思？！\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/14
msgid ""
"Based on the projected number of incoming\n"
"warheads,\n"
msgstr ""
"根据预测的来袭\n"
"弹头数量，\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/15
msgid ""
"Washington D.C. is presumed destroyed.\n"
msgstr ""
"华盛顿特区推定已被摧毁。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/16
msgid ""
"The President is most likely dead, the U.S.\n"
"government's control lost.\n"
msgstr ""
"总统很可能已经死亡，美国\n"
"政府已失去控制。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/17
msgid ""
"I realize that. So why not retaliate?!\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道。那为何不报复？！\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/18
msgid ""
"With both sides destroyed, global anarchy would\n"
"ensue.\n"
msgstr ""
"双方被毁后，全球将陷入\n"
"无政府状态。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/19
msgid ""
"Recovery would be... difficult.\n"
msgstr ""
"恢复将……极为困难。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/20
msgid ""
"The United States' nuclear strike capability must\n"
"therefore be neutralized\n"
msgstr ""
"因此，美国的核打击能力必须\n"
"被消除，\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/21
msgid ""
"in order to preserve the Communist bloc, where\n"
"government remains largely intact.\n"
msgstr ""
"以保全共产主义阵营，那里\n"
"政府大体上仍然完好。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/22
msgid ""
"You're siding with the enemy? You can't be serious!\n"
msgstr ""
"你站在敌人那边？你不是认真的吧！\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/23
msgid ""
"...Tell me, how do you define enemy?\n"
msgstr ""
"……你如何定义敌人？\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/24
msgid ""
"There are no borders in this world.\n"
msgstr ""
"这世上没有国界。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/25
msgid ""
"The same conclusion, again and again... Where is\n"
"the flaw?\n"
msgstr ""
"同样结论，一次又一次……破绽\n"
"在哪？\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/26
msgid ""
"All right. Let's try something else. Commencing test.\n"
msgstr ""
"好吧。换个方式。开始测试。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/27
msgid ""
"Understood.\n"
msgstr ""
"明白。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/28
msgid ""
"...You're crossing a suspension bridge.\n"
msgstr ""
"……你正走过一座吊桥。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/29
msgid ""
"Is this my mission?\n"
msgstr ""
"这是我任务？\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/30
msgid ""
"Yes. Your destination is the other side.\n"
msgstr ""
"对。你的目的地是对岸。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/31
msgid ""
"The bridge is wide enough for only one person to\n"
"pass at a time.\n"
msgstr ""
"这座桥很窄，一次只能让一个人\n"
"通过。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/32
msgid ""
"A man is approaching from the opposite side. He's\n"
"carrying a gun.\n"
msgstr ""
"对面有个人正在靠近。他\n"
"手里拿着一把枪。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/33
msgid ""
"I shoot him.\n"
msgstr ""
"我开枪打他。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/34
msgid ""
"Suppose he's your husband?\n"
msgstr ""
"假如他是你丈夫？\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/35
msgid ""
"...I shoot him.\n"
msgstr ""
"……我开枪打他。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/36
msgid ""
"In self defense?\n"
msgstr ""
"自卫？\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/37
msgid ""
"To spare him the grief. One must die, and one\n"
"must live.\n"
msgstr ""
"免他悲伤。必须死一个，活\n"
"一个。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/38
msgid ""
"...Next question.\n"
msgstr ""
"……下一个问题。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/39
msgid ""
"Your father asks you to fix the roof and mow the\n"
"lawn.\n"
msgstr ""
"你父亲让你去修屋顶，还要修剪\n"
"草坪。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/40
msgid ""
"When you climb the ladder onto the roof, the\n"
"ladder is taken away.\n"
msgstr ""
"当你爬上梯子到屋顶时，梯子\n"
"被拿走了。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/41
msgid ""
"I fix the roof.\n"
msgstr ""
"我修屋顶。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/42
msgid ""
"And when you're finished?\n"
msgstr ""
"修完之后呢？\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/43
msgid ""
"I jump down.\n"
msgstr ""
"我跳下去。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/44
msgid ""
"You'll break more than bones at this height.\n"
msgstr ""
"这个高度，断的不只是骨头。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/45
msgid ""
"I see no need to change my decision. I have not\n"
"finished mowing the lawn.\n"
msgstr ""
"我看没必要改变我的决定。我还没\n"
"修剪完草坪。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/46
msgid ""
"I must remain loyal to the mission.\n"
msgstr ""
"我必须忠于任务。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/47
msgid ""
"...Next.\n"
msgstr ""
"……下一个。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/48
msgid ""
"There is a snake in the bushes. It is poisonous. I\n"
"need you to get rid of it.\n"
msgstr ""
"灌木丛里有一条蛇。它有毒。我\n"
"需要你去把它除掉。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/49
msgid ""
"I chase it back to its nest.\n"
msgstr ""
"我追它回巢。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/50
msgid ""
"You can't. The snake's too vicious. It's already\n"
"killed many people.\n"
msgstr ""
"你做不到。那条蛇太凶残了。它已经\n"
"杀了好多人。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/51
msgid ""
"...I chase it away.\n"
msgstr ""
"……我把它赶走。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/52
msgid ""
"It will bite you unless you kill it.\n"
msgstr ""
"你不杀它，它就会咬你。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/53
msgid ""
"Go home!\n"
msgstr ""
"回家去！\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/54
msgid ""
"...Kill me... Kill me now...\n"
msgstr ""
"……杀了我……现在就杀了我……\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/55
msgid ""
"Why not kill the snake? Your mission is to get rid\n"
"of it.\n"
msgstr ""
"为何不杀蛇？任务就是\n"
"除掉它。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/56
msgid ""
"Is this what you call loyalty?\n"
msgstr ""
"这就是你说的忠诚？\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/57
msgid ""
"What are you loyal to? Country? Ideology?\n"
"Feelings?\n"
msgstr ""
"你忠于啥？国家？思想？\n"
"感情？\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/58
msgid ""
"I... I...\n"
msgstr ""
"我……我……\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/59
msgid ""
"I am loyal to myself.\n"
msgstr ""
"我忠于自己。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/60
msgid ""
"...Who's there?!\n"
msgstr ""
"……谁？！\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/61
msgid ""
"Who's that?!\n"
msgstr ""
"谁？！\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/62
msgid ""
"Intruder!\n"
msgstr ""
"有入侵者！\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/0
msgid ""
"I'm about to leave for Costa Rica, a place\n"
"completely unfamiliar to me.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/1
msgid ""
"And on a top-secret mission for the CIA, no less.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/2
msgid ""
"No guarantees I'll come back alive. Might even get\n"
"rubbed out by the CIA itself.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/3
msgid ""
"So I'm leaving behind this record, for her sake... for\n"
"The Boss' honor.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/4
msgid ""
"Ever since I was a child, I've loved to look up at\n"
"the night sky.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/5
msgid ""
"I'd go outside after sunset and drink in the cold air.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/6
msgid ""
"The moon, Venus, so many stars floating on the\n"
"edge of infinity...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/7
msgid ""
"In Manchester, it wasn't very often you saw the\n"
"night sky in all its star-studded glory.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/8
msgid ""
"But it was enough to stir a deep longing inside me.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/9
msgid ""
"Even as others cowered beneath Nazi air raids,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/10
msgid ""
"I was out there watching the skies, dreaming of\n"
"one day reaching the heavens.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/11
msgid ""
"There were, of course, more practical concerns.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/12
msgid ""
"My skin was incredibly sensitive. Even the slightest\n"
"bit of sun would turn it an angry shade of red.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/13
msgid ""
"Playing outside during the day was completely out\n"
"of the question.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/14
msgid ""
"Naturally, I hardly ever had the chance to play with\n"
"other children my age.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/15
msgid ""
"But I never felt lonely for it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/16
msgid ""
"Their way of thinking was irrational, making them\n"
"simple, easy to predict.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/17
msgid ""
"The boys would talk of tanks and aeroplanes and\n"
"creepy, crawly bugs...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/18
msgid ""
"the girls of pretty dresses, glass beads and tea\n"
"and cakes. Of boys they liked...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/19
msgid ""
"I never had much to say on such matters.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/20
msgid ""
"The curious thing is, adults really aren't all that\n"
"different.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/21
msgid ""
"They're simple, capricious. Especially men.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/22
msgid ""
"As they get older, their heads fill with thoughts of\n"
"women and more women.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/23
msgid ""
"Thankfully, I always did have a head for\n"
"mathematics.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/24
msgid ""
"When I was about ten, I'd visit a Dr. Turing, who\n"
"lived nearby.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/25
msgid ""
"We'd sit and discuss mathematical logic.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/26
msgid ""
"The lights were always on at his house, even in the\n"
"dead of night.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/27
msgid ""
"\"Theoretically,\" he'd say, \"there's no algorithm that\n"
"a computing machine couldn't reproduce.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/28
msgid ""
"Dr. Turing wasn't foolish like other men,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/29
msgid ""
"although I didn't find out why until later... after he\n"
"died.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/30
msgid ""
"\"The time will come,\" he'd say, \"when computers will\n"
"be able to think for themselves.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/31
msgid ""
"That idea rocked me to my core.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/32
msgid ""
"My aptitude for mathematics brought me closer to\n"
"the stars.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/33
msgid ""
"I breezed through school, then went to America for\n"
"university.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/34
msgid ""
"While I was studying at Caltech, NASA was\n"
"established.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/35
msgid ""
"I signed up in a heartbeat.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/36
msgid ""
"I was a pretty good computer engineer at the time,\n"
"and NASA needed skills like mine.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/37
msgid ""
"The work was enjoyable. Even though I'd given up\n"
"on going into space myself,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/38
msgid ""
"it was a pleasure just being a part of it all.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/39
msgid ""
"I was assigned to Project Mercury, America's effort\n"
"to compete with the Soviets in manned space flight.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/40
msgid ""
"Seven men were chosen as pilot candidates for\n"
"the program,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/41
msgid ""
"becoming heroes overnight. People called them the\n"
"\"Mercury Seven.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/42
msgid ""
"The project made good progress, more or less. We\n"
"had all the funds and materials we needed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/43
msgid ""
"After countless hours of analysis, we even had\n"
"plans for something on par with Sputnik.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/44
msgid ""
"We thought it'd be only a matter of time before we\n"
"caught up with the Russians.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/59
msgid "w"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/74
msgid ","
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/80
msgid "ki|Ӫ"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/82
msgid "~"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/0
msgid ""
"I spoke out against her going,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/1
msgid ""
"submitting a report stating the ray shielding was\n"
"inadequate.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/2
msgid ""
"But the brass's response was brusque:\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/3
msgid ""
"\"She's already been exposed to a nuclear test in\n"
"Nevada. She's the perfect candidate.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/4
msgid ""
"It was completely irrational.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/5
msgid ""
"Repeated exposure to radiation would only\n"
"increase the danger.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/6
msgid ""
"But the government was still reeling from the\n"
"Soviets' success with Sputnik.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/7
msgid ""
"There was no hope of getting a rational response.\n"
"They were simply too panicked.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/8
msgid ""
"People can be so obtuse when it comes to things\n"
"they can't see.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/9
msgid ""
"I, however, understood all too well.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/10
msgid ""
"Just as invisible ultraviolet radiation scorched my\n"
"skin,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/11
msgid ""
"heavy particle radiation from space would cause\n"
"irreparable harm to human tissue.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/12
msgid ""
"In a word, she was expendable.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/13
msgid ""
"It was during The Boss's pre-flight checkup\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/14
msgid ""
"that I noticed something strange on the X-ray of\n"
"her skull.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/15
msgid ""
"Part of the right hemisphere of her brain was\n"
"damaged.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/16
msgid ""
"It seemed inexplicable given her keen intelligence\n"
"and amazing physical prowess.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/17
msgid ""
"But there it was, and I decided to report it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/18
msgid ""
"I hoped that perhaps my discovery of a physical\n"
"defect\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/19
msgid ""
"would result in the flight being canceled.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/20
msgid ""
"...But as I went to make my report, she stopped me.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/21
msgid ""
"\"Why?\" I demanded. \"How can you let yourself be\n"
"their guinea pig?!\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/22
msgid ""
"Ignoring my protests, she took me up to the roof\n"
"of the lab.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/23
msgid ""
"The night sky was ablaze with stars.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/24
msgid ""
"It was there that I learned how she had wounded\n"
"her head.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/25
msgid ""
"1943, Los Alamos.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/29
msgid "$"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/99
msgid "Lwt"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/0
msgid ""
"The days that followed were spent training\n"
"tirelessly for our first space flight.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/1
msgid ""
"The Boss endured conditioning that tested the\n"
"limits of human capability,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/2
msgid ""
"and I supported her. Those were happy days.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/3
msgid ""
"On April 12th, the spacecraft carrying The Boss\n"
"left the Earth's atmosphere.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/4
msgid ""
"Although it was only 20 minutes of ballistic flight,\n"
"it was nothing short of miraculous,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/5
msgid ""
"considering how little time we'd had. The first\n"
"human in space. We were ecstatic.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/6
msgid ""
"Then something went wrong.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/7
msgid ""
"The reentry angle was slightly off, warping the\n"
"outer hull.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/8
msgid ""
"The cause was clear - it was the\n"
"hastily-constructed window we'd installed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/9
msgid ""
"Her capsule missed the projected splashdown point\n"
"by a long shot.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/10
msgid ""
"As we raced towards the capsule, a breaking news\n"
"broadcast came over the radio.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/11
msgid ""
"It was the news report of the successful launch of\n"
"the Vostock rocket,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/12
msgid ""
"piloted by the cosmonaut Yuri Gagarin. They'd\n"
"beaten us into space by the slimmest of margins.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/13
msgid ""
"When we arrived, the capsule had already\n"
"disappeared beneath the waves.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/14
msgid ""
"The Boss was floating on the surface.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/15
msgid ""
"I... can't really recall what happened next.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/16
msgid ""
"They told me later that I gave a strange scream\n"
"and plunged into the sea,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/17
msgid ""
"not caring whether my skin would burn.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/18
msgid ""
"She didn't wake up.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/19
msgid ""
"Her entire body was bruised, burnt, scorched by\n"
"cosmic rays.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/20
#: codec/1/284/0x11c2d0/5
msgid ""
"It was a miracle she was still alive.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/21
msgid ""
"Every day, propaganda boasting of the shining\n"
"accomplishment flowed out of the Soviet Union.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/22
msgid ""
"The hardest part was having to read the report\n"
"the next morning from Izvestia,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/23
msgid ""
"the Soviet governmental paper.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/24
msgid ""
"Written there after the report were those\n"
"legendary words of Major Gargarin -\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/25
msgid ""
"\"The Earth is blue.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/26
msgid ""
"The person who should have said those words,\n"
"though, was incapacitated, confined to a bed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/27
msgid ""
"NASA opted to pretend the flight had never\n"
"happened.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/28
msgid ""
"The Soviets had orbited a man around the Earth\n"
"and returned him safely.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/29
msgid ""
"We'd barely managed to escape the atmosphere\n"
"and achieve ballistic flight.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/30
msgid ""
"Even worse, the pilot was horribly mangled and\n"
"the spacecraft lost altogether...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/31
msgid ""
"As they saw it,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/32
msgid ""
"covering it up was the only alternative to seeing\n"
"the nation's pride dealt yet another blow.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/33
msgid ""
"I've been told\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/34
msgid ""
"military records show The Boss was taking part in\n"
"the Bay of Pigs incident at the time.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/35
msgid ""
"They were that desperate to erase the whole affair.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/36
msgid ""
"In the end,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/37
msgid ""
"Alan Shepard's ballistic flight one month later\n"
"became known as America's first space flight.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/38
msgid ""
"Shepard's flight owed its success to insights\n"
"earned through The Boss's sacrifice.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/39
msgid ""
"But to me, none of that mattered. I prayed day and\n"
"night for her recovery,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/40
msgid ""
"never leaving her side, not even for a moment.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/41
msgid ""
"Then, as summer ended and the chill of winter\n"
"approached, she spoke.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/42
msgid ""
"\"Give me water...\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/43
msgid ""
"I threw myself on her breast, and she embraced me.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/44
msgid ""
"It was all I needed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/45
msgid ""
"I thought she would tell me about space.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/46
msgid ""
"The true sky, where the stars don't twinkle.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/47
msgid ""
"But the only thing she'd speak of was Earth.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/48
msgid ""
"Our home - as she'd seen it from space. So\n"
"fleeting, so irreplaceable.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/49
msgid ""
"I was ashamed. I'd been enamored for so long with\n"
"the sky that\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/50
msgid ""
"I'd never thought to look beneath my feet... at the\n"
"ground upon which I stood.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/51
msgid ""
"As soon as her rehab was over, she was gone.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/52
msgid ""
"It happened without warning. No one informed me,\n"
"and the higher-ups wouldn't say a word.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/53
msgid ""
"It wasn't so strange or surprising, really.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/54
msgid ""
"I simply assumed she was off to complete her next\n"
"mission.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/0
msgid ""
"Enter simulation date.\n"
msgstr ""
"输入模拟日期。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/1
msgid ""
"August 24.\n"
msgstr ""
"8月24日。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/2
msgid ""
"Location?\n"
msgstr ""
"地点？\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/3
msgid ""
"Tselinoyarsk, USSR.\n"
msgstr ""
"苏联，采利诺亚尔斯克。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/4
msgid ""
"Mission?\n"
msgstr ""
"任务？\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/5
msgid ""
"Support a covert agent whose objective is the\n"
"rescue of a nuclear weapons scientist.\n"
msgstr ""
"支援一名秘密特工，其目标是\n"
"营救一名核武器科学家。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/6
msgid ""
"Who is the agent?\n"
msgstr ""
"特工是谁？\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/7
msgid ""
"Your student. Your... most beloved...\n"
msgstr ""
"你学生。你最爱的……\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/8
msgid ""
"...Acknowledged. Define current mission progress.\n"
msgstr ""
"……明白。说明当前任务进展。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/9
msgid ""
"With your help, the agent has successfully made\n"
"contact with the target.\n"
msgstr ""
"在你的帮助下，特工成功\n"
"与目标取得了联系。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/10
msgid ""
"All that's left is to wait for recovery.\n"
msgstr ""
"剩下的就是等待接应。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/11
msgid ""
"Now, deduce the best course of action.\n"
msgstr ""
"现在，推断最佳行动方案。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/12
msgid ""
"...I take the scientist away from the agent.\n"
msgstr ""
"……我从特工手中带走科学家。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/14
msgid ""
"As a gift when I defect.\n"
msgstr ""
"叛逃献礼。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/15
msgid ""
"...Why are you defecting?\n"
msgstr ""
"……你为何叛逃？\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/16
msgid ""
"To reform my Special Forces unit with my former\n"
"comrades-in-arms.\n"
msgstr ""
"重组我的特种部队，与我的前战友们\n"
"并肩作战。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/17
msgid ""
"NO! I don't want to know your objective. I'm asking\n"
"for the reason.\n"
msgstr ""
"不！我不想知道你的目标。我问的是\n"
"原因。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/18
msgid ""
"Why are you betraying your country?\n"
msgstr ""
"你为何背叛你的国家？\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/19
msgid ""
"...I do not defect in order to betray America.\n"
msgstr ""
"……我叛逃并非为背叛美国。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/20
msgid ""
"Betrayal is merely the outcome of that defection.\n"
msgstr ""
"背叛只是叛逃的结果。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/21
msgid ""
"Response time is always slower here...\n"
msgstr ""
"这里响应总是更慢……\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/22
msgid ""
"Perhaps she lacks confidence in her judgment.\n"
msgstr ""
"也许她对自己的判断缺乏信心。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/23
msgid ""
"You're a hero in the West. Why should the Soviets\n"
"trust you?\n"
msgstr ""
"你在西方是个英雄。苏联人凭什么\n"
"信任你？\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/24
msgid ""
"In addition to the scientist,\n"
msgstr ""
"除科学家外，\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/25
msgid ""
"I provide them with a portable nuclear warhead\n"
msgstr ""
"我还提供一枚便携核弹头\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/26
msgid ""
"in order to win the favor of a Russian GRU officer.\n"
msgstr ""
"以博取一名苏联GRU军官的欢心。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/27
msgid ""
"...And then you launched it.\n"
msgstr ""
"……然后你发射了。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/28
msgid ""
"Launched... the nuke? Me?\n"
msgstr ""
"发射……核弹？我？\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/29
msgid ""
"That's right. At a target inside Soviet territory.\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。目标是苏联境内。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/30
msgid ""
"Nuclear weapons... make my blood run cold. They\n"
"blot out the future. How... could I...?\n"
msgstr ""
"核武器……让我胆寒。它们\n"
"抹杀未来。我……怎能……？\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/31
msgid ""
"Karma... Is... is it my karma?\n"
msgstr ""
"业……这……这是我的业吗？\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/32
msgid ""
"The karma my mistake has brought upon us... My...\n"
"My...\n"
msgstr ""
"我错给我们的业……我的……\n"
"我的……\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/33
msgid ""
"Attention. Discontinue forward reasoning.\n"
"Cross-check with knowledge base.\n"
msgstr ""
"注意。停止向前推理。\n"
"与知识库交叉核对。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/34
#: codec/1/265/0x109080/40
msgid ""
"Affirmative.\n"
msgstr ""
"确认。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/35
msgid ""
"...Cross-check complete. Revising conclusion as\n"
"follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"……交叉核对完成。修正结论\n"
"如下：\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/36
msgid ""
"I steal the new weapons developed by the scientist\n"
msgstr ""
"我偷走科学家研发的新武器\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/37
msgid ""
"and then launch the nuke at the weapons design\n"
"bureau.\n"
msgstr ""
"然后向武器设计局发射核弹。\n"
"\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/38
msgid ""
"Forward and backward reasoning are in conflict...\n"
msgstr ""
"正向与反向推理冲突……\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/39
msgid ""
"Attention. Return to forward reasoning.\n"
msgstr ""
"注意。回到正向推理。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/41
msgid ""
"...Your apprentice returns for the scientist.\n"
msgstr ""
"……你的徒弟回来找科学家了。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/42
msgid ""
"I send him away.\n"
msgstr ""
"我赶走他。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/43
msgid ""
"He doesn't give up.\n"
msgstr ""
"他不肯放弃。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/44
msgid ""
"I send my comrades to defeat him.\n"
msgstr ""
"我派同伴去击败他。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/45
msgid ""
"All of them fail.\n"
msgstr ""
"全失败了。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/46
msgid ""
"Even the GRU officer who oversaw your defection\n"
"is defeated by your apprentice\n"
msgstr ""
"连监督你叛逃的格鲁乌军官\n"
"也被你的徒弟击败\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/47
msgid ""
"- along with the new weapon.\n"
msgstr ""
"连同新武器。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/48
msgid ""
"Now, what is your course of action?\n"
msgstr ""
"那么，你会怎么做？\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/49
msgid ""
"...I fight him.\n"
msgstr ""
"……我跟他打。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/50
msgid ""
"Why? With your GRU patron dead, there's no\n"
"reason for you to fight.\n"
msgstr ""
"为啥？格鲁乌靠山已死，\n"
"你没理由再打。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/51
msgid ""
"Why not just run away?\n"
msgstr ""
"何不一走了之？\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/52
msgid ""
"I... must fight him.\n"
msgstr ""
"我……必须跟他打。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/53
msgid ""
"I do not see the reason. With a solider of your\n"
"caliber on his side,\n"
msgstr ""
"我想不通。以你这种身手的士兵\n"
"在他那边，\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/54
msgid ""
"how could the GRU officer be defeated to begin\n"
"with? Did you betray him, too?\n"
msgstr ""
"格鲁乌军官怎么可能被击败？\n"
"你也背叛了他？\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/55
msgid ""
"I... I've been waiting... for a long time.\n"
msgstr ""
"我……我已经等了……很久。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/56
msgid ""
"You could switch allegiance from GRU to KGB,\n"
msgstr ""
"你可以从格鲁乌转投克格勃，\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/57
msgid ""
"and take the remaining nuke as a gift.\n"
msgstr ""
"把剩下的核弹当见面礼。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/58
msgid ""
"There's no chance they wouldn't welcome a hero\n"
"of your stature.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们绝不会拒绝你这种\n"
"级别的英雄。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/59
msgid ""
"Drift away. My place is with them now.\n"
msgstr ""
"走吧。我归宿跟他们一起。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/60
msgid ""
"I didn't ask you that! Give me the basis for your\n"
"reasoning! Tell me the truth...\n"
msgstr ""
"我没问这个！给我你推理的依据！\n"
"说实话……\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/61
msgid ""
"Politics determine who you face on the battlefield.\n"
msgstr ""
"政治决定你在战场上面对谁。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/62
msgid ""
"Why won't you answer me?! It's like you were just\n"
"waiting for him to kill you!\n"
msgstr ""
"你为什么不回答我？！\n"
"简直像在等他杀你！\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/63
msgid ""
"I was disloyal... Betrayed my country... I deserve to\n"
"die...\n"
msgstr ""
"我不忠……背叛了我的国家……我该死……\n"
"\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/64
msgid ""
"How can you say that?! You can't be a traitor!\n"
"You're not that kind of person!\n"
msgstr ""
"你怎么能这么说？！你不可能是叛徒！\n"
"你不是那种人！\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/65
msgid ""
"Kill me... Kill me now...\n"
msgstr ""
"杀了我……现在就杀了我……\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/66
msgid ""
"STOP IT! STOP IT! Attention! Discontinue reasoning!!\n"
msgstr ""
"住手！住手！注意！停止推理！！\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/67
msgid ""
"One must die, and one must live...\n"
msgstr ""
"一人得死，一人得活……\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/68
msgid ""
"Stop it, damn you! DISCONTINUE!\n"
msgstr ""
"住手，该死的！停止！\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/69
msgid ""
"Life's end... Isn't it beautiful...?\n"
msgstr ""
"生命的终结……不美吗……？\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/70
msgid ""
"SHUT DOWN!!\n"
msgstr ""
"关机！\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/71
msgid ""
"...Always in the same place, her reasoning goes\n"
"haywire.\n"
msgstr ""
"……总在同一处，她推理就\n"
"出错。\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/72
msgid ""
"Someone holds the key... Perhaps it's him...\n"
msgstr ""
"有人握着钥匙……也许是他……\n"

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/73
msgid ""
"I'll get it out of him. One way or another...!\n"
msgstr ""
"我会撬开他嘴。不管怎样……！\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/0
msgid ""
"As of today I will be living here at Mother Base.\n"
"Now my real trial begins.\n"
msgstr ""
"从今天起我就住在母基地了。\n"
"现在真正的考验开始了。\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/1
msgid ""
"Zadornov was paying my room, board, and tuition,\n"
msgstr ""
"扎多尔诺夫付我的食宿和学费，\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/2
msgid ""
"but he has since been captured.\n"
msgstr ""
"但他后来被抓了。\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/3
msgid ""
"I told the man that with no more money from the\n"
"KGB,\n"
msgstr ""
"我告诉那人，KGB\n"
"不再给钱了，\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/4
msgid ""
"I could no longer afford school.\n"
msgstr ""
"我再也上不起学了。\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/5
msgid ""
"...He bought my story, and when I said I would be\n"
"willing to work,\n"
msgstr ""
"……他相信了我的说辞，当我说我\n"
"愿意工作时，\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/6
msgid ""
"he took pity on me and let me stay.\n"
msgstr ""
"他可怜我，让我留下。\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/7
msgid ""
"For some reason Miller really plead my case.\n"
msgstr ""
"不知为何米勒真替我求了情。\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/8
msgid ""
"That was helpful, but the man is still a fool.\n"
msgstr ""
"那有用，但这人还是个蠢货。\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/9
msgid ""
"His men are no better.\n"
msgstr ""
"他手下也一样。\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/10
msgid ""
"They think their training makes them strong,\n"
msgstr ""
"他们以为训练让他们变强，\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/11
msgid ""
"but that kind of strength is nothing in the face of\n"
"true power.\n"
msgstr ""
"但那种力量在\n"
"真正的力量面前不值一提。\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/12
msgid ""
"And better yet, they wait on me hand and foot,\n"
msgstr ""
"更妙的是，他们对我百般伺候，\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/13
msgid ""
"believing I am just a schoolgirl.\n"
msgstr ""
"以为我只是个女学生。\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/14
msgid ""
"Looks like I won't be working too hard, after all.\n"
msgstr ""
"看来我不用太辛苦。\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/15
msgid ""
"Just today,\n"
msgstr ""
"今天，\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/16
msgid ""
"while scouting out the living quarters,\n"
msgstr ""
"我侦察生活区时，\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/17
msgid ""
"I saw a group of them in the corner of the deck\n"
"making a fuss.\n"
msgstr ""
"看到甲板角落有一群人\n"
"在闹腾。\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/18
msgid ""
"Going over for a look, I saw they were feeding a\n"
"kitten.\n"
msgstr ""
"我过去一看，他们在喂\n"
"一只小猫。\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/19
msgid ""
"A bunch of grown, hard men, and they are the\n"
"ones acting like schoolgirls!\n"
msgstr ""
"一群粗壮的硬汉，\n"
"却像女学生一样！\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/20
msgid ""
"\"Look, isn't he cute?\" What is wrong with them?\n"
msgstr ""
"“看，它多可爱？”他们有病吧？\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/21
msgid ""
"Disgusted, I just nodded and smiled.\n"
msgstr ""
"我嫌恶地点点头笑笑。\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/22
msgid ""
"I must stay in character, after all.\n"
msgstr ""
"毕竟我得演好角色。\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/23
msgid ""
"I indulged their chit-chat for a few moments,\n"
msgstr ""
"我陪他们闲聊了几句，\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/24
msgid ""
"then one of them asked me to give the thing a\n"
"name.\n"
msgstr ""
"然后有人让我给那东西\n"
"起个名。\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/25
msgid ""
"They had just taken it from its mother.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们刚把它从母猫身边拿走。\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/26
msgid ""
"I named it Nuke.\n"
msgstr ""
"我给它起名核弹。\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/27
msgid ""
"I improvised some nonsense about how\n"
msgstr ""
"我随口编了句胡话，说\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/28
msgid ""
"\"our compassion for living things can help prevent\n"
"wars.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"“对生命的怜悯能防止\n"
"战争。”\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/29
msgid ""
"The men gave me a little fish.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们给我条小鱼。\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/30
msgid ""
"I held it out in my palm, and the kitten happily ate\n"
"it up.\n"
msgstr ""
"我摊在手心，小猫高兴地\n"
"吃了。\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/31
msgid ""
"What a pathetic... feeble creature.\n"
msgstr ""
"多可悲……软弱生物。\n"

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/32
msgid ""
"It sickens me.\n"
msgstr ""
"真恶心。\n"

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/0
msgid ""
"Today Chico invited me to go fishing with the\n"
"soldiers.\n"
msgstr ""
"今天奇科邀我和士兵们\n"
"去钓鱼。\n"

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/1
msgid ""
"I suppose finding one's own food does have its\n"
"merit,\n"
msgstr ""
"自己找食物或许有\n"
"好处，\n"

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/2
msgid ""
"but I prefer not to be involved in such a degrading\n"
"task.\n"
msgstr ""
"但我不想干这种\n"
"丢人的事。\n"

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/3
msgid ""
"And their prattling on about fishing being \"fun\" is\n"
"nonsense.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们唠叨钓鱼多“好玩”，\n"
"纯属胡扯。\n"

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/4
msgid ""
"I'm not here to find playmates.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不是来找玩伴的。\n"

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/5
msgid ""
"Nevertheless, distasteful as it was,\n"
msgstr ""
"尽管如此，虽然恶心，\n"

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/6
msgid ""
"I went along in order to maintain my cover.\n"
msgstr ""
"我为了维持伪装才跟去的。\n"

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/7
msgid ""
"Chico thrust a fishing pole into my hands, and we\n"
"went up onto the deck,\n"
msgstr ""
"奇科把一根鱼竿塞进我手里，我们\n"
"走上了甲板，\n"

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/8
msgid ""
"where several soldiers had gathered.\n"
msgstr ""
"那里聚着几个士兵。\n"

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/9
msgid ""
"They welcomed us warmly.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们热情地欢迎我们。\n"

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/10
msgid ""
"With so few women aboard Mother Base, I'm\n"
"treated like a princess.\n"
msgstr ""
"母基地女人少，我\n"
"被当公主对待。\n"

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/11
msgid ""
"No one suspects I'm neither a teenager nor a\n"
"student.\n"
msgstr ""
"没人怀疑我既不是少女也不是\n"
"学生。\n"

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/12
msgid ""
"It was nice and sunny,\n"
msgstr ""
"天气晴朗，\n"

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/13
msgid ""
"with a gentle breeze and waves.\n"
msgstr ""
"微风轻拂，波浪轻摇。\n"

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/14
msgid ""
"As I cast my line and waited for a bite,\n"
msgstr ""
"我抛下鱼线等鱼上钩，\n"
